 q="다음 글의 요지로 가장 적절한 것은?",
 passage="We often praise children for being 'smart' when they succeed. The intention is kind, but the message can backfire. A child told that success reflects a fixed trait learns that failure must reflect the absence of that trait. Faced with a harder problem, such a child may avoid it altogether rather than risk evidence that she is not smart after all. Praise directed at effort and strategy, by contrast, frames difficulty as part of the process rather than a verdict on ability.",
